ChatSched — Claude fixes, Sept 2
=================================

Scope: this file documents ONLY the second task resolved from
"Claude To fix 1..txt" — item 6, CRITICAL: Public publisher rows expose
sensitive columns. Item 5 (admin role escalation) was already completed
and documented separately in "claude fixes Sept 1". Items 7 onward in
that file were left untouched.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. What the finding said, verified against the real source
------------------------------------------------------------------------
publishers_select_approved_or_own_or_admin (schema_phase5.sql):
    for select using (status = 'approved' or auth.uid() = user_id or public.is_admin())
This has no `to authenticated` restriction, so it applies to the `anon`
role too. It's a ROW filter only — once any row passes it (which every
approved publisher always does, for literally anyone), the ENTIRE row
becomes readable through PostgREST, including every sensitive column the
table has accumulated since schema_phase5.sql first added the policy:
email, mobile_number, company_registration, vat_number, admin_notes,
rejected_reason, business_name (schema_phase5.sql), and payout_method,
payout_details, payout_account_verified_at (schema_payouts_phase1.sql).
This is real and independent of any frontend file: an unauthenticated
`GET /rest/v1/publishers?select=*&status=eq.approved` returns all of it
today, regardless of what any UI chooses to render.

